Is centroid size an absolute measure of size? My data is 3D bill shape and I want to know if centroid size is a measure of absolute bill size or bill size relative to body size. I'm hoping centroid size is a measure of the latter to account for instances where small birds have big bills relative to their body size (like some of the Darwin's finches for example). If not, how could I get this metric?

